  "id": "expressive-language-disorder",
  "term": "expressive language disorder",
  "definition": "Expressive language disorder is a condition in which a person’s ability to develop or use spoken or other expressive language is impaired relative to their nonverbal thinking and their ability to understand language. It may arise after brain injury or trauma, or occur developmentally without a known neurological cause.",
